================================================================================
CLINICAL & MEDICAL DEVICE DISCLAIMER (MANDATORY TERMS OF USE)
================================================================================

1. NOT A CERTIFIED MEDICAL DEVICE:
   Cardiac Analyst is an academic research and educational technology prototype.
   It has NOT been evaluated, cleared, approved, or certified by the United
   States Food and Drug Administration (FDA), the European Medicines Agency (EMA),
   the Central Drugs Standard Control Organisation (CDSCO), or any other
   national or international medical regulatory authority.

2. NO CLINICAL DIAGNOSIS OR INDEPENDENT MEDICAL DECISION-MAKING:
   This Software and its machine learning outputs (including but not limited to
   electrocardiographic condition scores, rhythm evaluations, interval calculations,
   vitals risk stratifications, and triage recommendations) do NOT constitute
   medical advice, clinical diagnosis, patient management plans, or treatment
   prescriptions. 

3. INDEPENDENT QUALIFIED CLINICAL OVERSIGHT:
   Any health decisions, diagnoses, emergency interventions, or pharmaceutical
   prescriptions must be evaluated and made independently by licensed and
   qualified healthcare professionals. Do NOT rely on model scores, automated
   triage classifications, or software outputs to rule out acute cardiovascular
   emergencies (including acute myocardial infarction or critical arrhythmias).

4. EMERGENCY SITUATIONS:
   In any emergency situation, acute chest pain, shortness of breath, or medical
   crisis, immediately contact local emergency medical services (such as 112 in
   India or 911 in the United States) or present to the nearest hospital
   emergency department.
